{
  "id": "breakwater",
  "name": "The Breakwater",
  "description": "A small upstairs grill at the far end of the Strand's old pier, past where the boardwalk crowd thins out. Dark wood panelling, a plank floor, white enamel lamps over a few small tables, and a counter onto a little kitchen with a flat-top grill and hanging pans. One long run of old steel-framed windows looks out over the black bay: the harbour cranes and their lights, stacked containers, the city's towers, and to the left the Low Roller turning on its pier. In the corner by the window, a booth in worn oxblood vinyl, set for two, with a candle lamp.",
